     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day (2,000 mg/day for extended-release), and it raises the risk of lactic acidosis. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum single dose of 1,000 mg.\n\nPossible intended orders include:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day in divided doses**, such as 850 mg twice daily with meals\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n\nIf you do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
